1. DEFINITIONS

"NodOS" means the software in this repository, in source or compiled form,
together with its documentation, artwork, name and logo.

"Licensor" means the NodOS copyright holders and maintainers.

"You" means anyone using, copying, modifying or sharing NodOS.

"Derivative" means any work that is based on, copied from, translated from, or
includes any part of NodOS, including modified versions, forks, ports,
rewrites that follow its code or structure, plugins, images, packages and
anything that bundles or ships NodOS.

"Commercial Use" means any use of NodOS or a Derivative that earns, or is meant
or able to earn, money or any other payment, benefit, advantage or value for
anyone, directly or indirectly. It includes, without limit:

  (a) selling, licensing, renting, leasing or reselling NodOS or a Derivative,
      or charging for a copy, download, update, key, activation, build, mirror
      or access, including "cost recovery" or "handling" charges;
  (b) offering NodOS or a Derivative as, or inside, a paid or ad-supported
      service, hosted product, managed service, subscription, "premium" tier,
      trial that leads to payment, or feature gate;
  (c) charging for support, installation, setup, configuration, integration,
      consulting, training, customization, monitoring or maintenance of NodOS or
      a Derivative, or using NodOS to deliver any paid service to a client;
  (d) including NodOS or a Derivative in a product, device, appliance, image,
      distribution, template or service that is sold or otherwise earns
      revenue, even if NodOS is not the part being charged for;
  (e) earning from advertising, sponsorship, affiliate links, paywalls, tips
      or donations that unlock anything, memberships, or data collection placed
      on or around NodOS or a Derivative, or on a site, repository, video,
      channel or account whose purpose is to distribute or promote it;
  (f) charging for access to a Derivative's source code, builds or releases;
  (g) using NodOS, its code or its documentation to build, train, fine-tune or
      market a product or service that is sold or earns revenue;
  (h) any use by or for a business, company, sole trader or other for-profit
      organization, or by anyone in the course of their paid work, other than
      under written permission from the Licensor.

2. WHO MAY USE IT, AND HOW

Subject to this whole license, you may, free of charge, and only if your use is
not Commercial Use:

  (a) use NodOS on your own equipment for personal, household, hobby, learning,
      research or volunteer purposes, and likewise in a school, university,
      charity or other non-profit organization, or a public body, that does not
      charge for what NodOS is used for;
  (b) download, read, copy and study the source code;
  (c) modify the source code and build your own versions for use under (a);
  (d) share NodOS and your Derivatives with anyone, in source and compiled
      form, as long as it is free and you follow section 3.

The Licensor may give written permission for a use that this license does not
allow. Permission has to be in writing, names who and what it covers, and does
not change this license for anyone else.

3. CONDITIONS

  (a) Free only. You may not charge for NodOS or any Derivative, or make
      Commercial Use of either, and you may not help, enable or knowingly
      supply someone who does.
  (b) Same license. Every copy and Derivative you share must include this
      license text and the copyright notice and must be under this same license.
      You may not add, remove or change terms, relicense, or sublicense under
      different terms.
  (c) Source stays public. A Derivative you share, in any form, must come with
      its complete source, published openly and free of charge.
  (d) Notices stay. You may not remove, hide or alter copyright notices,
      license text, attribution or the NOTICE file. A Derivative must credit
      NodOS and its authors in its README and in its about or version output.
  (e) Modified means labeled. A modified version must say clearly, in its name
      and in its documentation, that it is modified, by whom, and that it is not
      the official NodOS.
  (f) No passing off. You may not use the NodOS name, logo or release signing
      key, or anything confusingly similar, so as to suggest that your
      Derivative is official or endorsed. See docs/legal/trademarks.md.
  (g) No circumvention. You may not remove, weaken or bypass the update
      signature check, run a look-alike update channel, or distribute builds
      that pretend to be official ones.
  (h) No misuse. You may not use NodOS to attack, break into or disrupt systems
      you do not own or have permission to manage.

